WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.656
Evidence at Source keeps facts about a migrant worker in the worker's own wallet.

00:00:05.656 --> 00:00:09.220
It's a fictional demo that runs entirely in the browser.

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:16.800
An agency or a factory signs each fact, but it only counts once the worker counter-signs.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.234
After that, changing any number breaks the pair.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.808
A bank's AI agent asks to check them.

00:00:23.808 --> 00:00:28.270
The worker sees that it can only get yes-or-no answers, and allows it.

00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:31.624
Every query passes three gates.

00:00:31.624 --> 00:00:41.819
The first checks the agent's authority and institution on a vLEI chain, our own simulation rather than GLEIF's live system, and a forged root fails.

00:00:43.041 --> 00:00:46.624
Only yes-or-no answers and group rates get through.

00:00:46.624 --> 00:00:56.391
The bank's agent sees three trues and a recommendation for human review; the brand's sees 85 percent across 20 workers, but no one's hours.

00:00:57.904 --> 00:01:05.844
When the worker leaves the country, their credentials are revoked, and the credential gate stops the bank's agent before it reads anything.

00:01:07.635 --> 00:01:08.722
We attack it too.

00:01:08.722 --> 00:01:19.025
A planted instruction changes nothing, because no language model makes the call, and a second query that would single out five workers by subtraction is refused.

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:24.328
Evidence at Source: the agents get answers, not data.
